EXT. CABLE CAR GONDOLA - HIGH OVER A HARBOR - NIGHT

A glass bubble swinging a hundred meters above black water. City lights fall away in every direction. Wind leans on the cabin.

The gondola has stopped. Dead stop. It sways.

CALLUM DRUMMOND-OKAFOR, 30s, rumpled tuxedo, bow tie undone, grips the handrail. SUNITA RAO, 30s, bridesmaid's dress the color of a bruised plum, heels in one hand, leans against the opposite glass.

CALLUM
We're fine.

SUNITA
We are not fine. We are stuck.

CALLUM
Stuck is a kind of fine.

Silence. The cabin sways. They both grab the rail. Eyes meet. Both freeze.

SUNITA
You look terrible.

CALLUM
You left the wedding.

SUNITA
You followed me.

CALLUM
Also terrible, I know.

A speaker crackles near the ceiling.

REYES (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Gondola four, this is control. Are you hurt? Over.

CALLUM
(to the speaker)
No. Just stuck. Are we going to move?

REYES (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Power's out on the whole peak. Twenty minutes. Maybe thirty. Please sit down.

Sunita sits on the bench. Callum sits across from her. Their knees almost touch.

SUNITA
Twenty minutes.

CALLUM
I can count to twenty minutes of anything.

SUNITA
You said that about your marriage.

His mouth twitches. A pained half-smile.

CALLUM
Twelve minutes in, I'll have thought of something good.

Light blooms in the next gondola, thirty feet away, swaying. A silhouette stands at the glass, waving both arms.

FELIX ODUYA, 30s, in a groom's white jacket, pounds on the glass of the adjacent cabin and mouths words.

SUNITA
(without turning)
Don't look.

CALLUM
Is that --

SUNITA
Don't.

Felix cups his hands against the glass. Shouts. Muffled, through two walls of glass and a gale.

FELIX (O.S.)
(muffled)
SUNITA! I CAN EXPLAIN!

Callum and Sunita both stand. They crash together at the center of the cabin, arguing, then not arguing, her hand fisted in his lapel, his on her wrist, then her jaw. The gondola lurches.

They fall back to the bench, laughing, helpless, horrified.

SUNITA
I can't believe he's the groom.

CALLUM
I can't believe you're the one who brought the ring.

REYES (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Gondola four? I'm hearing a lot of shouting. Everyone okay?

SUNITA
(to the speaker)
Never better.

The lights flicker on. The cable shudders. The gondola begins, slowly, to move, toward the shore, toward the other cabin, toward whatever comes next.

Callum offers her his hand. She takes it.
